  "question": {
    "text": "<p>For the adsorption of hydrogen on platinum, the activation energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;and for the adsorption of hydrogen on nickel, the activation energy is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>41</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>kJ</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>&#8211;</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>.</mo></math> The logarithm of the ratio of the rates of chemisorption on equal areas of the metals at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>300</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></math> is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi><mi>_</mi></math>&nbsp;(Nearest integer)</p><p>Given:&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>In</mi><mn>10</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">J</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>mol</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math></p>"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "2",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>According&nbsp; to Arrhenius&#39;s equation,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>Ae</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mo>/</mo><mi>RT</mi></mrow></msup><mspace linebreak=\"newline\"></mspace><mi>logk</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>logA</mi><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi></msub><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>RT</mi></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo></math>For the adsorption of hydrogen on platinum, the activation energy</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo></math>for the adsorption of hydrogen on nickel, the activation energy</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>log</mi><mfenced><mfrac><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mrow><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">a</mi><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>RT</mi></mrow></mfrac></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>11</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>1000</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>300</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>990</mn><mo>&#8776;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p></blockquote>"
